do not read a ROM the core is going to open itself

`LibretroCore::load` read every ROM into memory and kept it in `self.rom` for
the life of the game, then handed the core a pointer to it. gpSP never looks
at that pointer: it sets `need_fullpath`, takes the path and opens the file
itself. slot has never asked about the flag.

So a gpSP game cost its own size twice over -- 8 MB for Kirby, 16 for Golden
Sun -- and Mother 3's 32 MB simply could not be loaded on a handheld with
about 40 MB free. "mother 3 crashed it on load", which is what sent me
looking. mGBA does want the data, and still gets it.

`retro_get_system_info` is bound for the one field this needs, and the data
pointer is null when nothing was read rather than pointing at an empty Vec.

This is worth more than everything else freed today put together, and it was
found by reading the load path after a cart failed rather than by the memory
work that preceded it -- which is an argument for reading the obvious path
first.

